    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "No stale references. The change is complete and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made `householdId` deterministic and reworked everything keyed off the household to use it. `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n- **`OwnerHousehold.java`** \u2014 replaced the address-based, creation-order-dependent derivation with a deterministic `idFor(lastName, postcode)`: the first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode`. Returns `null` when no postcode (an owner with no postcode has no household). Dropped the now-unused `resolve`/`normalizeAddress`.\n\n- **`AssignOwnerHousehold.java`** \u2014 now simply stamps the deterministic `householdId` onto the owner (no housemate scan, no back-fill, since the id is order-independent). Every owner with the same lastName+postcode gets the same id automatically.\n\n- **`EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity.java`** \u2014 is now the **household duplicate block**: if any existing owner already carries the request's computed `householdId`, it responds **409** \u2014 *unless* `sharesHousehold` is set, which bypasses the block and lets the owner be created as a declared household member.\n\n- **`AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 excludes owners sharing the same `householdId` from the soft-match, so a declared household member is **not** flagged as a possible duplicate (a declared member is not a suspected duplicate).\n\n- **`DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`**, the `POST` YAML comments, and the OpenAPI descriptions for `sharesHousehold`/`householdId` were updated to describe the new deterministic, (lastName, postcode)-keyed behaviour.\n\n`AssignOwnerHouseholdSize` already counted by `owner.getHouseholdId()`, so with the id now deterministic and set before save, the household-size input (and thus the membership level wiring) keys off the computed householdId with no further change.\n\nThe new acceptance test (`coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId`) passes: same lastName+postcode \u2192 same `householdId` (second owner admitted via `sharesHousehold`), different lastName \u2192 different `householdId`.",
